0,Cocama language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocama_language,"January 1, 2026 - It is spoken along the banks of the Northeastern lower Ucayali, lower Marañón, and Huallaga rivers and in neighboring areas of Brazil and an isolated area in Colombia. There are three dialects. The robust dialect is known as Cocama, Kokama, Kukama-Kukamiria, Ucayali, Xibitaoan, Huallaga, ...",Kukama-Kukamiria,Tupian
1,Supporting the Kukama: Songs from Silence | A sponsored silence in solidarity with a struggling language.,https://kukamasongsfromsilence.wordpress.com/,"A musical group, “IKARA” which means “Song” is writing and recording music expressing their desire to protect the rainforest and their culture, dedicating their songs to the “Shapishico”, the soul of the rainforest. The Kukamas-Kukamirias, also called “hombres de agua” (men of water) came from along the River Marañon, taking advantage of Nature’s cycles, without damaging the rainforest.",Kukama-Kukamiria,Tupian
